                    {
                        "translation_id": "79bc1941-e95e-4158-8a1b-959d5daddfb0",
                        "source_entry_id": "a219ab4c-5e6e-3a56-9110-1031cc6bdf64",
                        "source_sense_id": "3a616244-a731-3f4f-bc1d-a9d81ec9d258",
                        "source_sense_description": "een kerkelijke straf",
                        "target_lang_word": "anathema",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anathema",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee8a839d-15d8-3571-8c30-abf8d932d0ec",
                                        "entry_id": "36bcd60b-af85-33ee-8c61-d8728ed69c0b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ban or curse pronounced with religious solemnity by ecclesiastical authority, often accompanied by excommunication; something denounced as accursed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "21545811-59e6-3426-9bb9-fdd7e85d7b25",
                                        "entry_id": "36bcd60b-af85-33ee-8c61-d8728ed69c0b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something which is vehemently disliked by somebody."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27007a4b-c2ea-4d68-8d5d-6e52acfba08b",
                                                "sense_id": "21545811-59e6-3426-9bb9-fdd7e85d7b25",
                                                "text": "Even three years ago, the thought of spending two hours, let alone a whole day, without my mobile would have been anathema."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4550716d-0373-4858-8182-fe24495d1855",
                                                "sense_id": "21545811-59e6-3426-9bb9-fdd7e85d7b25",
                                                "text": "The actor, who prizes mystery, hated being gossip fodder. “That was anathema to him,” said his sister Martha Fiennes, a filmmaker, “and he just hated the curiosity into his life.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29fc45b9-67cd-4350-aea3-1078c141715c",
                                                "sense_id": "21545811-59e6-3426-9bb9-fdd7e85d7b25",
                                                "text": "To law enforcement officers injured in the Jan. 6 mayhem, as well as members of Congress and others present in the Capitol that day who feared for their lives, such adulation for convicted rioters is not only misguided but also anathema to a civilized society."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "371ac82e-4969-3827-b326-617a9bae6b3b",
                                        "entry_id": "36bcd60b-af85-33ee-8c61-d8728ed69c0b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An imprecation; a curse; a malediction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab87c3b3-1e19-4857-821d-9952d1870b1a",
                                                "sense_id": "371ac82e-4969-3827-b326-617a9bae6b3b",
                                                "text": "I trembled at his ringing wealth\nOf manifold anathemas […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "100f5eaf-b76a-4a8d-944f-aa1a4eeee0e3",
                                                "sense_id": "371ac82e-4969-3827-b326-617a9bae6b3b",
                                                "text": "That was a curse from which no flight was possible: the anathema of a man who had once known holiness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41bbbcb2-571c-4e0f-8e88-42159f7f0106",
                                                "sense_id": "371ac82e-4969-3827-b326-617a9bae6b3b",
                                                "text": "“Assumptions are anathema to communication.” “You're anathema. Fine, all right, I messed up. I guess I'll go break her stupid heart since that's what you all seem to want.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7cd39553-b450-37e5-8326-fbc5bb40a18b",
                                        "entry_id": "36bcd60b-af85-33ee-8c61-d8728ed69c0b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any person or thing anathematized, or cursed by ecclesiastical authority to unending punishment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a08c9b97-4955-4326-bab6-148c01e60691",
                                                "sense_id": "7cd39553-b450-37e5-8326-fbc5bb40a18b",
                                                "text": "If any one refuses to confess that the Word of God the Father is united in hypostasis to flesh, and is one Christ with His own flesh, the same being at once both God and man, let him be anathema."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b316b83a-5651-421f-8e98-8b5b08826a16",
                                                "sense_id": "7cd39553-b450-37e5-8326-fbc5bb40a18b",
                                                "text": "If any man love not the Lord Jesus Christ, let him be Anathema Maranatha."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c99aa20e-bd41-4a7c-9f7b-ad59fa421989",
                                                "sense_id": "7cd39553-b450-37e5-8326-fbc5bb40a18b",
                                                "text": "Ἆνάθεμα, accurẛed, חרם, which the Septuagint renders Anathema, ẛignifies Perẛons or Things devoted to Deẛtruction and Extermination. The Jewiẛh Nation were now an Anathema, deẛtin'd to Deẛtruction. St. Paul to expreẛs his Affection to them, ẛays, he could wiẛh to ẛave them from it, to become an Anathema and be deẛtroy'd himẛelf."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1f7d1ff1-f804-40bb-af82-1ac14f4b5d54",
                        "source_entry_id": "a219ab4c-5e6e-3a56-9110-1031cc6bdf64",
                        "source_sense_id": "3a616244-a731-3f4f-bc1d-a9d81ec9d258",
                        "source_sense_description": "een kerkelijke straf",
                        "target_lang_word": "anathème",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anathème",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2668d777-88b8-3df9-a127-14ce928cf82a",
                                        "entry_id": "474d2c3c-6c98-3555-8847-76db9751ac7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sentence de malédiction qui retranche de la communion de l’Église."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12d937fa-b740-4a86-9e74-259d60ea64e8",
                                                "sense_id": "2668d777-88b8-3df9-a127-14ce928cf82a",
                                                "text": "L’affaire fut au cœur des discussions du IIIᵉ concile du Latran réuni en 1179, qui condamna par l’anathème les hérétiques et leurs soutiens : le canon 27 contient un appel à prendre les armes et promet déjà aux défenseurs de l’orthodoxie la rémission de tous leurs péchés, un véritable privilège de croisade."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9da7e634-5e23-4ec4-ace3-affabcf478e5",
                                                "sense_id": "2668d777-88b8-3df9-a127-14ce928cf82a",
                                                "text": "Si quelqu’un dit que tous les chrétiens ont le pouvoir d’annoncer la parole de Dieu et d’administrer les sacrements ; qu’il soit anathème."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29c5b5a0-e532-4e9c-b1dc-018b3f547c06",
                                                "sense_id": "2668d777-88b8-3df9-a127-14ce928cf82a",
                                                "text": "Alors il étendit les bras du côté de Sion ; et, la taille droite, le visage en arrière, les poings fermés, lui jeta un anathème, croyant que les mots avaient un pouvoir effectif."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1ca2688-ae4b-49a4-97f0-fbfa05a77c4c",
                                                "sense_id": "2668d777-88b8-3df9-a127-14ce928cf82a",
                                                "text": "Heureusement, messieurs, nous ne sommes plus au temps où l’on pouvait s’émouvoir des anathèmes perfectionnés que le Syllabus prodigue à ceux qui le méconnaissent, et nous ne ferons pas aux républicains, même les plus timides, l’injure de croire qu’ils puissent se déterminer par des arguments de ce genre."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a286e4b1-e11d-34e8-9ec1-c2c0143e982f",
                                        "entry_id": "474d2c3c-6c98-3555-8847-76db9751ac7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Réprobation ; blâme solennel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "formal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0595241-eb49-486a-999d-d954a7ce0bd3",
                                                "sense_id": "a286e4b1-e11d-34e8-9ec1-c2c0143e982f",
                                                "text": "La bonne compagnie de Verrières commençait à s’indigner de ce que ses anathèmes faisaient si peu d’impression sur M. de Rênal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75cb5e37-96d0-479a-9f2d-8fe365b3f5d4",
                                                "sense_id": "a286e4b1-e11d-34e8-9ec1-c2c0143e982f",
                                                "text": "Don Ramon courba la tête sous cet anathème ; le front pâle et l’âme remplie de remords cuisants, il rentra lentement dans l’hacienda."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa7d5c9e-d957-4a8f-afe7-7f60c4696244",
                                                "sense_id": "a286e4b1-e11d-34e8-9ec1-c2c0143e982f",
                                                "text": "C'était toujours des anathèmes épouvantables contre ceux qui étaient justement en train de lui lécher le cul, des gâtés-pourris-crasse qui se demandaient avec des airs ténébreux de quoi ils pourraient bien avoir envie dans la vie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5059b76b-a504-42df-802c-7f8880bab800",
                                                "sense_id": "a286e4b1-e11d-34e8-9ec1-c2c0143e982f",
                                                "text": "Les ulémas lancent anathème sur anathème : « malheur à qui s’associera à eux, malheur à qui mangera à leur table, malheur à qui s’unira à eux par le mariage, verser leur sang est aussi légitime que d’arroser son jardin »."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b58c499-63ea-390a-b545-5d640037bb5e",
                                        "entry_id": "474d2c3c-6c98-3555-8847-76db9751ac7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne qui est un objet d’opprobre, d’exécration."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31947b15-60cb-444a-aac5-f1f9f6d313c6",
                                                "sense_id": "4b58c499-63ea-390a-b545-5d640037bb5e",
                                                "text": "Car c’est une loi singulière que ce peuple d’anathèmes n’ait pu assumer la réprobation collective dont il s’honore qu’au prix fabuleux du protagonisme éventuel de l’individu."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
